EVIDENCE CONFLICTS (must resolve, do not average)
==================================================
1. CVE-2025-31277: RESOLVED 2026-11-10, TWICE. (a) Via upstream source:
   retraction doc's "JIT — DEAD" row was wrong about the mechanism (fix
   commit 716536ce98d6 shows a runtime bug in JSGlobalObjectInlines.h;
   regression test = P1077's trigger verbatim). (b) Via LIVE TEST: P1077
   ran on the PS5 09:23 UTC — post-HABT match arrays use slow-put (length
   grows on OOB-index writes), 0 corruption, 0 leaks, VULN:false. The
   retraction row's CONCLUSION ("DEAD") stands, its REASON was wrong
   (not "JIT absent" — the engine respects HABT; Sony backported or
   equivalent). CVE label caveat: CVE-2025-31277 was Apple's May 2025
   advisory; the commit is Oct 2025, so the true CVE id may differ.
2. P927 (2026-11-09) claims ASLR defeat + lineDash arbitrary R/W bus;
   the 2026-11-10 retraction scorecard says arbitrary read NOT ACHIEVED and
   retracts the FontFace leak family. Treat P927 as unverified until
   replicated with sentinel controls.
3. P1069v3 "leak=yes" (2026-11-10 08:27 UTC): RESOLVED by P1069v7/v9 —
   the leak is the FontFace 'then'-getter UAF spraying zero-init ABs;
   engine heap pointers land at +0x58/+0x68 of a reclaimed 192-byte
   object. Real, repeatable (v9: 5/5), per-process ASLR-tracked. This is
   a verified step-4 heap-pointer disclosure. It is NOT the retracted
   P1043 mechanism (that was self-written header bytes in a parse path).

